### Layout Plan
Use the underexposed photos full-bleed. Lean into the low-light aesthetic by heavily crushing the blacks and allowing the grain to act as a texture mask. 

Anchor the design with two large, semi-transparent blocks (Neon Pink and Acid Cyan) placed off-center, intersecting in the middle third of the canvas. Setting these blocks to `mix-blend-mode: screen` allows the photo’s grain to bleed through the color.

Set the primary typography in a massive, heavy sans-serif. Break the text across multiple lines to form a solid graphic shape. Position the text so it overlaps the background, the pink block, and the cyan block. Applying `mix-blend-mode: difference` (or `exclusion`) to Voltage Yellow text forces it to dynamically invert colors wherever it crosses boundaries, turning magenta or deep blue depending on the layers beneath it.

